From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jianfeng Liu <Jianfeng.Liu@cixtech.com>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 16:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 42/92] usb: cdns3: fix spin lock issue in suspend/resume

cdns_resume() may sleep (it talks to the controller and the PHY), so it
must not be invoked with cdns->lock held.  Acquire the lock only after
the resume call returns, before updating cdns->in_lpm.

The cdnsp-pci.c and cdnsp-plat.c parts of the original patch are gone:
upstream removed the cdnsp-pci PM ops entirely, and the cdnsp-plat.c
hunk is folded into 0025 which now creates that file.

Signed-off-by: Jianfeng Liu <Jianfeng.Liu@cixtech.com>
---
 drivers/usb/cdns3/cdns3-plat.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdns3-plat.c b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdns3-plat.c
index bb5405460..d4c23d07e 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdns3-plat.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdns3-plat.c
@@ -292,8 +292,10 @@ static int cdns3_controller_resume(struct device *dev, pm_message_t msg)
 
 	cdns3_set_platform_suspend(cdns->dev, false, false);
 
-	spin_lock_irqsave(&cdns->lock, flags);
+	/* cdns_resume() may sleep; do not invoke it under cdns->lock. */
 	cdns_resume(cdns);
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&cdns->lock, flags);
 	cdns->in_lpm = false;
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&cdns->lock, flags);
 	cdns_set_active(cdns, !PMSG_IS_AUTO(msg));
